message: "If you use this software or its associated research outputs, please cite the repository using the metadata below."

title: "Generalizable Ensemble Deep Learning for Dermoscopic Skin-Lesion Classification: Internal Evaluation on HAM10000 and External Evaluation on ISIC 2019"

authors:
  - family-names: "Saykat"
    given-names: "Md Naim Hassan"
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science, Université Paris-Saclay"
    email: "mdnaimhassansaykat@gmail.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-5270-3970"

abstract: >
  Reproducible evaluation framework for seven-class dermoscopic skin-lesion
  classification. Seven archived HAM10000-trained models (a custom CNN,
  ResNet-50, DenseNet-121, EfficientNet-B3, ConvNeXt-Tiny, MobileNetV3-Large,
  and ViT-B/16) and their equal-weight probability ensemble are evaluated on a
  standardized 2,003-image HAM10000 cohort and on ISIC 2019. Because ISIC 2019
  contains the HAM10000 images, external results are also reported on the
  15,320 ISIC 2019 images that no model saw during training. The repository
  provides the evaluation code with the audited preprocessing and class
  ordering of each checkpoint, statistical comparisons, calibration analysis
  with post-hoc temperature scaling, computational-cost measurements,
  qualitative Grad-CAM attribution, and curated result tables and figures.

